k='lem-dj-bridge-murphy-cellular-basis-and-cell-form';after[k]['strategy']=proofs['standalone-murphy-proof.md'];after[k]['deps']=list(dict.fromkeys(after[k]['deps']+[helper,'cor-sum-of-squares-of-standard-tableau-numbers','lem-dj-bridge-sign-automorphism-and-star-dual']));after[k]['statement']=after[k]['statement'].replace('=\\dim S^\\lambda_{\\mathbb Q(q)}','')
k='lem-dj-bridge-integral-murphy-and-polytabloid-straightening';after[k]['strategy']=proofs['constructive-proof.md'];after[k]['deps']=list(dict.fromkeys(after[k]['deps']+[helper]));after[k]['statement']=r'''Over $A=\mathbb Z[q^{\pm1}]$ and after base change to every commutative $R$ with $q\in R^\times$, put $\mu=\lambda\prime$. The actual ordinary polytabloid module $P(\lambda)=z_\lambda H$ is free with basis $e_t=z_\lambda T_{d_\mu(t)}$ indexed by $t\in\operatorname{Std}(\mu)$, and its inclusion in $M(\lambda)$ is split as an $R$-module inclusion. Each $e_t$ has row-tabloid support weakly dominated by $t\prime$, with coefficient $q^{\ell(d_\mu(t))}$ on that transpose-standard row tabloid. This gives an explicit unit triangular embedding minor. Exact signed Garnir relations $z_\lambda\sum_{d\in S_\alpha\cap D_\mu}\theta(T_d)=0$ for the specified $\mu$-Garnir belts, with coefficients determined by the finite coset formula in the proof, and finite row-standard straightening survive all base changes. The Gram matrix of the restricted DJ form is obtained from this embedding and the row weights: if $e_t=\sum_r a_{r,t}b_r$, then $B_{tu}=\sum_r a_{r,t}a_{r,u}q^{\ell(d_\lambda(r))}$. Unit triangularity concerns the embedding, not the Gram matrix; the DJ form can degenerate. The independent standalone Murphy cellular proof supplies the signed cell quotient used for spanning. No generic semisimple dimension count establishes this integral assertion; the split unit minor and a square surjection with right inverse prove it over the ground ring. No choice principle is used.'''.replace('\\lambda\\prime','\\lambda\'').replace('t\\prime','t\'')
